A module with no CSS still records its library. `a` depends on `c` only
through `b`, and `b` has no `[%css]`. All three are in library `mylib`.

  $ cat > a.ml <<EOF
  > let a = [%css "color: blue"]
  > let _ = B.b
  > EOF

  $ cat > b.ml <<EOF
  > let b = C.c
  > EOF

  $ cat > c.ml <<EOF
  > let c = [%css "color: red"]
  > EOF

`b` gets a `[@@@css.config]` with its library and nothing else.

  $ ../../standalone.exe -cookie 'library-name="mylib"' --impl b.ml
  [@@@css.config [("library-name", "mylib")]]
  let b = C.c

Without the cookie, `b` gets no attribute.

  $ ../../standalone.exe --impl b.ml
  let b = C.c

  $ for m in a b c; do ../../standalone.exe -cookie 'library-name="mylib"' --impl $m.ml --dump-ast -o $m.pp.ml; done

So `b` groups with `mylib`, not with its directory: one group, no cycle,
and `c`'s rule comes before `a`'s.

  $ styled-ppx.generate --log debug a.pp.ml b.pp.ml c.pp.ml
  styled-ppx: output file: stdout
  styled-ppx: library order: mylib
  styled-ppx: order: mylib: C, B, A
  styled-ppx: edge: B -> C
  styled-ppx: edge: A -> B
  styled-ppx: environment: development
  styled-ppx: stylesheet:
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  ._a_4ekvmb{color:red;}
  ._a_4esm7b{color:blue;}
  
